\section*{Introduction}
Traditional   KYC is   often slow, kind of repetitive and expensive in a way that 
banks didn't really optimize. Many teams spend 48--72 hours for each customer,  
ask multiple times for   the same   documents and depend a lot on  human review.  
Cost sits somewhere around \$8--12 (₹650–₹950), yet fraud still slips thru and  
some outcomes feel inconsistent.

AegisKYC tries to  re-engineer the workflow into an AI–first style pipeline.  
By mixing document   intelligence, biometric auth,   behaviral analytics, device  
risk scoring and decisioning, the   whole verification time kinda drops to 
\textbf{8--12 minutes}. Fraud catching improves to about \textbf{98.5\%}, and  
costs go down to \textbf{\$0.15 (₹12)}.  
This doc explains how the solution kind of works, why each layer   is there,  
and how it fits a smooth, compliant and scalable onboarding idea.

\section*{System Architecture Overview}
AegisKYC follows  a five–layer architecture:  
\textbf{Frontend → Application → Business Logic Microservices → AI/ML Engine → Database}.  
Each layer is  built for modularity, less latency, compliance, and some  
level of transparency.

\begin{figure}[h!]
    \centering
    \includegraphics[width=\linewidth]{SystemArchUpdated.png}
    \caption{System Architecture}
\end{figure}

\section*{1. Frontend Layer: User Interaction and Data Capture}
\textbf{Role:} Captures inputs and tries making them usable and clean for  
downstream AI systems.

\textbf{How it works:}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1cm]
    \item HTML5 + Tailwind gives a smoother UI but sometimes loads differently on devices.
    \item Validation runs in real–time so users usually know if the doc is blurry or not.
    \item MediaStream API records selfie + some liveness prompts right inside browser.
    \item WebGL/Canvas pull device fingerprint entropy for fraud scoring (not perfect but good).
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Why it matters:}  
Better input quality avoids repeated re-uploading and reduces errors later.

\section*{2. Application Layer: Routing, Orchestration, and API Control}
\textbf{Role:} This layer basically connects everything and sends data where it should go.

\textbf{How it works:}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1cm]
    \item Flask + Waitress WSGI handle API calls with okay latency.
    \item API groups: \texttt{/auth}, \texttt{/kyc}, \texttt{/admin}, \texttt{/org}.
    \item JWT sessions protect interactions but sometimes tokens expire early.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Why it matters:}  
It makes the flow structured so modules don’t mix concerns randomly.

\section*{3. Business Logic Layer: Modular Microservices}
This area runs rules, checks, thresholds, and leaves proper trails required  
for compliant KYC.

\textbf{Key modules:}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1cm]
    \item \textbf{auth\_service:} Does login and checks credentials correctness.
    \item \textbf{kyc\_verification\_service:} Runs 7-step KYC process end to end.
    \item \textbf{identity\_vault:} Keeps encrypted PII using AES-256-GCM.
    \item \textbf{document\_validator:} Ensures IDs follow shape + clarity rules.
    \item \textbf{face\_matching:} Looks for similarity between selfie and ID photo.
    \item \textbf{risk\_aggregation:} Combines signals into one score (sometimes swings).
    \item \textbf{manual\_review\_queue:} Stores escalated edge cases.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Why it matters:}  
Regulators prefer clear separation of duties so this helps with explainability.

\section*{4. AI/ML Engine: Document, Biometric, and Risk Intelligence}

\subsection*{4.1 Document Intelligence}
\textbf{How it works:}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1cm]
    \item Tesseract OCR extracts fields at about \textbf{95.7\% accuracy}.
    \item Pre-processing checks blur, shadows, exposure and weird corners.
    \item Tamper detection catches forged or manipulated areas.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Impact:}  
Automates a big chunk of manual document reading.

\subsection*{4.2 Biometric Verification}
\textbf{Components:}
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1cm]
    \item Liveness checks (blinks/micro-movement).
    \item CNN-based deepfake detector at \textbf{98.5\% accuracy}.
    \item Face match must cross \textbf{85\% threshold}.
\end{itemize}

\textbf{Impact:}  
Stops impersonation + synthetic identities.

\subsection*{4.3 Behavioral Intelligence}
\textbf{Signals captured:}  
typing rhythm, keystroke delays, scroll smoothness,   mouse curvature  
and hesitation pauses. Not always perfect but usually useful.

\textbf{Impact:}  
Adds another hidden layer of human verification.

